{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall say: Moreover, your servant Jacob is behind us.</b> He commanded that each of them say this statement in addition to the particular message assigned to him, so that Esau would find all their words directed to this end — that Jacob was coming behind them to Seir, to meet his brother." "<b>For he said: I will appease his face with the gift.</b> He put these words in the mouth of his servants in order to diminish Esau's fury through the language of submission together with the gift." "<b>I will see his face.</b> This is the manner of visitation proper for nobles, as in יֵרָאֶה כָל זְכוּרְךָ אֶת פְּנֵי הָאָדוֹן (Exodus 23:17), וְלֹא יֵרָאוּ פָנַי רֵיקָם. So too he later said to Esau: כִּי עַל כֵּן רָאִיתִי פָנֶיךָ כִּרְאוֹת פְּנֵי אֱלֹהִים (Genesis 33:10), for it is the custom to visit nobles with a gift along with seeing their face."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {2 "The second quoted phrase, וְלֹא יֵרָאוּ פָנַי רֵיקָם, alludes to Exodus 34:20; Sforno gives no citation for it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:02.102909511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}